    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email is already in use by another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException`, thrown when a new owner's lower-cased email collides with an existing owner's.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` returning `409 Conflict` with `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the email (which already lower-cases it), it now checks all existing owners case-insensitively and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a match. The check is guarded so a null/absent email (email is optional) skips the uniqueness check.\n\nThe check follows the same pattern as the existing duplicate-telephone rule, and the acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (create owner, then create another with the same email \u2192 expect 409) passes.",
